<article class="env-lemma" id="0EPK">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EPK">Lemma <span data-tag="0EPK">42.33.4</span>.</a> Let $(S, \delta )$ be as in Situation <a href="/tag/02QL" data-tag="02QL">42.7.1</a>. Let $f : X \to Y$ and $g : Y \to Z$ be morphisms of schemes locally of finite type over $S$. Let $c \in A^ p(X \to Z)$ and assume $f$ is proper. Then the rule that to $Z' \to Z$ assigns $\alpha \longmapsto f'_*(c \cap \alpha )$ is a bivariant class denoted $f_* \circ c \in A^ p(Y \to Z)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Lemmas <a href="/tag/02R5" data-tag="02R5">42.12.2</a>, <a href="/tag/02RG" data-tag="02RG">42.15.1</a>, and <a href="/tag/02TA" data-tag="02TA">42.29.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>